FILED s514f (Opus, 2026-10-11) from the #3144 review probe (blessglob.pl): PRE-EXISTING on main 8f2fa11c, unchanged by #3144.

`->can('print')` on an UNBLESSED open filehandle answers TRUE in PCL; perl answers FALSE.

Reproducer (scratch/s514f/pr/can1.pl):
    open my $fh, "<", $0 or die;
    print ref($fh), " ", ($fh->can("print") ? "can" : "cannot"), "\n";
    my $g = \do { local *H }; open $g, "<", $0 or die;
    print ref($g), " ", ($g->can("print") ? "can" : "cannot"), "\n";

perl 5.40.3:  GLOB cannot / GLOB cannot
PCL:          GLOB can    / GLOB can

Perl: UNIVERSAL::can on an unblessed reference returns undef (the handle's IO::File method autoload applies to method CALLS, not to `can`, unless IO::File is loaded -- probe with `use IO::Handle` before fixing: then perl answers can).  PCL's `can` resolves the invocant through the same filehandle -> IO::Handle path as a method call.  Fix site: the `can` builtin's invocant-to-class step (UNIVERSAL::can); an unblessed ref answers undef unless the class is a loaded package.  Low value; filed per rule.
